Euler-brick K3 V': Frobenius trace computation
V' = {a^2+b^2=d^2, b^2+c^2=e^2, a^2+c^2=f^2} ⊂ P^5

p    | #V'(F_p)  | 1+p^2  | t = tr(Frob|H^2)
-----+-----------+--------+------------------
3    | 12       | 10    | 2/3
5    | 36       | 26    | 2
7    | 92       | 50    | 6
11    | 108       | 122    | -14/11
13    | 196       | 170    | 2
17    | 428       | 290    | 138/17
19    | 396       | 362    | 34/19
23    | 668       | 530    | 6

Note: K3 has b_2 = 22, so |t| <= 22.
Algebraic eigenvalues = p * (root of unity); contribute p, -p, or ±p·ζ_k.
Transcendental eigenvalues have |λ| = p but irrational.
